# Diagnostic Overlays

## Context
- When debugging visual game elements or physics interactions in real-time
- When optimizing performance and seeking to identify bottlenecks
- When developing complex game systems that require visual feedback
- When testing on devices where console logs are inaccessible
- When analyzing spatial relationships between game objects

## Requirements
- Create togglable visual overlays to display debugging information
- Implement performance monitors to track frame rates and execution times
- Display collision bounds, paths, and other physics information
- Visualize AI decision-making and pathfinding
- Ensure overlays can be easily toggled on/off by developers
- Design overlays to be minimally invasive to gameplay
- Include text displays for important numeric values and states
- Use color-coding for diagnostic clarity

